WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.567
The former

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.368
president, Donald Trump

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.636
had a lot to say tonight.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.270
Many,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.271
many of the things he said, of

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.107
course, were abjectly false.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.041
A torrent of falsehoods

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.642
even from the get go.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.977
CNN Sara Murray joins us now.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.780
Her job tonight is fact checking.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.782
So, Sara,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.384
I'm not going to ask you to fact check

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.319
everything he said that was false.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.721
Because we only have a couple more hours.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.525
But but what what strikes you?

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:26.960
Well, you know, look,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.628
I think one of the things off of the top

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.130
was that we heard

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.431
former President Trump again

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.599
say the election was rigged

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.733
and talk about ballot stuffing.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.834
And, look, the reality is

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.169
the election was not rigged.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:36.703
Biden won

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.505
by more than 7 million votes

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.739
and that ballot stuffing claim,

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.007
that was also bogus.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:41.574
Here is Trump's

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.876
false claim on this tonight.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.246
Out of the

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.280
people in this audience

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.315
and maybe a couple that don't.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.918
But most people understand what happened

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.420
that was a rigged election.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.320
And it's a shame

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.422
that we had to go through it.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.456
Can you publicly acknowledge

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.124
that you did lose the 2020 election?

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.659
Let me just go on.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.461
If you look at through the vote,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.430
they found millions of votes on camera

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.597
on government cameras

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.167
where they were stuffing ballot boxes.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.668
So with all of that,

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.670
I think it's a shame that what happened.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.104
I think it's

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.007
a very sad thing for our country.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.376
No, there is just no basis for this

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.310
claim. It is a lie.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:17.911
We have heard it.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.478
Trump claim

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.446
before that there was ballot

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.481
stuffing by election workers in Georgia.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.816
It has been debunked,

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.451
including by Republican election

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.618
officials in Georgia.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.554
There is no sign any illegality

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.456
like this occurred on a large scale

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:30.623
and multiple former Trump

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.158
officials, including Trump's own

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.960
former attorney general, Bill Barr,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.528
have said there was not sufficient fraud

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.163
to change the outcome of the 2020

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.765
election Jake. Yeah, and that true.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.901
The Vote Group is a group of unserious

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.970
right wing activists It is not

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:44.971
some sort of

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.241
objective election board.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.877
It's amazing to hear them cited

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.712
as some sort of source.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.714
Trump also claimed

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.783
he offered to send troops to the Capitol

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.784
on January six,

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.886
but House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.621
turned him down.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.190
I don't think that's true. Sir.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.125
No, not the case.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.693
I mean, Trump has tried to blame

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.094
former House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.729
for the violence on January six.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:10.663
He's falsely claimed

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.798
he ordered the National Guard

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.665
of the Capitol.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.433
So here is Trump's

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.269
attempt to rewrite history tonight.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.005
Says Miller wrote a book

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.673
and he's a fantastic guy

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.142
and he was ready to go.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.309
They turned him down.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.511
If you love the mayor

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.746
of Washington, D.C., lovely lady,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:27.947
she said.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:28.648
We don't want to

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.482
we don't like the look,

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.850
Nancy Pelosi said.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.285
We don't like the look.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.353
If they would have had just

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.588
I offered them 10,000 soldiers.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.457
I said, it could be ten.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.191
It could be more.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.025
But I offered them

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:41.227
specifically 10,000 soldiers.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.663
If they would have taken 500 soldiers,

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.864
you wouldn't have the problem.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:45.899
They turned it down

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.468
Here is the reality.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.036
The House speaker is not in charge

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.937
of Capitol security.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.205
That's the Capitol Police Board,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.740
which oversees the Capitol Police

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.308
and at the time of the riot

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.476
would have approved requests

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.977
for National Guard assistance.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:58.912
And here is former

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.080
acting Defense Secretary Chris Miller

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.749
telling the January six committee

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:03.950
that he was never given

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.052
an order by Trump to have 10,000 troops

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.253
ready to go to the Capitol

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.155
on January six.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.892
To be crystal clear, there was no direct

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.160
order from President Trump

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.528
to put 10,000 troops

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.296
to be on the ready

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.331
for January six crackdown.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.466
Yeah, that's correct.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.301
There was no direct

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.304
there was no order from the president.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:24.938
So, Jake,

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.439
as you can see, these claims by Trump

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.042
about January six, also false.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.744
Sara Murray thanks so much for that.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.513
I'm sure you're going to have more

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.380
fact checks for us

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.882
because there were more lies

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.350
than I could count

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.885
said by the former president.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.853
This evening let's talk about

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:44.757
one of the politically more impactful

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.160
decisions of his presidency

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.194
to put three conservatives

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.495
on the Supreme Court

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.730
that would ultimately overturn

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.931
Roe v Wade.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.266
And what he had to say

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.200
about that tonight.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.802
Kaitlan Collins was trying to get him

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.202
to say

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.270
whether he would sign

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.771
a national abortion ban

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.373
if he were reelected.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.041
He wouldn't really take a position.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.776
But here is what he said

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.679
about overturning Roe v Wade.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.184
I consider the other side to be radical

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.452
because the other side

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.319
under Roe v Wade

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.220
and other things,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.289
the other side, the radical,

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.691
because they will remember the debate

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.392
with Hillary Clinton.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.327
I said rip the baby out of the womb

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.829
at the end of the ninth month.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.964
They will kill the baby

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.299
in the ninth month.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.134
If you look at that crazy governor,

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.169
of Virginia from the former governor

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.538
where he said, no, the baby will be born

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.107
and then we'll decide essentially

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.341
whether or not to execute.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:35.575
Mr.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:35.842
President,

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.043
can we talk about what you would do?

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.278
But these are the radical people.

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:38.645
Like,

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:40.613
obviously,

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.582
he would rather talk about positions

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.616
that Hillary Clinton

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:46.552
never took than his own position, which

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.154
is not supported by polls.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:49.789
Just to be clear,

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.323
the things

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:50.723
you were saying about

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.892
Democrats are not true.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.960
Hillary Clinton did not say anything

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.962
about ripping the baby out of the womb.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.697
Let's just talk about the politics

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.799
of this Overturning Roe v Wade

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.368
is unpopular with the American people.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.469
It's unpopular with the voters.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.771
He needs to win the presidency

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.139
should he get the nomination.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.840
He doesn't want to talk about this.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.374
I don't know that

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.243
he's found a way to talk about it.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.644
Now, that was pretty clear tonight.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.780
And understandably,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.214
there are so much to unpack

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.382
in this town hall.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.351
But if he does get the nomination,

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:19.452
which is still a big if,

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:19.986
we're very,

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.622
very early in the process here,

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.357
he will have to face

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.225
a Democratic president

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.428
who has a White House and a campaign

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:31.030
who looks at the 2022 midterms

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.999
and believes that this is

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.269
exhibit A, B and C of why.

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.538
Yes, the economy is troubled. Yes.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.239
That there are questions about Joe Biden,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.941
but they still believe

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:44.877
that the abortion issue will drive voters

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.312
out to the polls.

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.647
To vote for Joe Biden

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:49.749
and to vote against Donald Trump.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:52.418
If you take all the other issues, maybe

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.586
even all the other noise

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:54.654
and you put them aside,

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:55.922
that is still front

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.623
and center in voters minds.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:01.294
And that answer, as you said, clearly,

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:02.061
if you are

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:04.430
the Trump campaign needs some refining.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.265
I don't know they can refine it

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.634
before the end of the primary season.

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:09.936
Perhaps he will do it

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.871
if he gets the general not even refining.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.474
I mean, he said I did that, I did that.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.975
And that is not what Michigan,

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.243
Wisconsin, Michigan,

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.444
Wisconsin, Pennsylvania

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.712
swing voters want.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.279
It seemed to me

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:21.447
that the goal tonight

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.081
for Trump

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.184
was to reinforce to conservative voters

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.987
that he supports the overturning of Roe

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:28.588
versus Wade.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.289
Now, he did that to a point

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:31.724
that might have actually produced

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:32.525
quite a number of

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.060
of general election ads.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.728
If he makes it to the general election.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:36.295
But I think that's

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.263
what they were trying to do,

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:37.930
because

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.198
part of the context here

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.100
is that in the weeks leading up to this,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.301
some of the reporting had been

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:42.802
that Trump's

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.872
aides were kind of saying or Trump

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.907
that was saying to his aides privately

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.809
that people like Ron DeSantis

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:51.310
had perhaps gone too far

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.112
with the six week abortion ban.

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.280
And when you saw Caitlin

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.149
pushing him on the date,

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.117
would he sign a federal abortion ban?

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:58.985
What weeks

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.053
would he support for an abortion ban?

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.357
He refused to answer those questions.

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:05.725
About the specifics.

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.293
They wanted to double down on

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.395
I support overturning Roe versus Wade

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:10.930
without getting him

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.199
tied down on anything concrete.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:14.934
That is, by the way, happening

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.536
right now in the States.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:18.404
These are not hypothetical situations.

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:19.138
And Trump

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.174
would not give the public

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:23.276
a clear answer about where he stands.

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.544
And in that respect

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:25.478
from the Trump campaign,

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:26.012
I'm sure

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:26.446
that they view

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.080
that as a victory in terms

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.882
of what he won in wanting to do

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:30.817
and how he executed.

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.385
Well, the phrase that he kept using

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:34.187
was it gave the Dobbs decision.

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:35.922
He called it a great victory.

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:36.722
He claimed,

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:37.156
of course,

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.224
that he had taken credit for it,

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:38.691
although, again,

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:39.692
if the Supreme Court

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.327
that actually ruled not the president.

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.361
Yeah, but he lived

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.898
He certainly did.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.433
But the issue he was saying

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:48.768
was it gave pro-lifers

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:50.169
something to negotiate with.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.838
Now, why that is so disingenuous,

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:52.705
is it one?

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:53.840
There were already trigger laws

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.441
that were on the books

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:58.211
that were created to be reinstated

00:07:58.211 --> 00:08:00.480
or implement new abortion related bans.

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:03.082
Should Roe v Wade ever be overturned?

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:03.616
Number two,

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:04.283
of course,

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:05.184
the negotiation,

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:07.086
he presumes, does not happen

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:08.788
because you have mifepristone

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:10.990
now on the virtual chopping block.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.926
You've got abortion bans under

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:16.729
partizan majorities in state legislatures

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.164
where there has been complaints

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:19.932
that there's no room to negotiate

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:21.133
on these very principles.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.935
And so this perception

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.270
that the Dobbs decision

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.872
by returning to the states

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:27.006
somehow affords

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:29.108
a greater opportunity to negotiate

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:30.810
is one not with the Supreme Court

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:31.777
really was think well,

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:32.712
they may think about it,

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:34.180
but they didn't actually just say, well,

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:34.714
but also not

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:36.215
